<Base title="About This Site | WIC Clinics" desc="What wicclinics.com is, where the data comes from, and why we are not the USDA.">
<main class="wrap">
  <h1 style="font-size:1.65rem">About this site</h1>
  <p class="lede">WIC Clinics is a <strong>private, independent</strong> reference site about the WIC program. We are not affiliated with the USDA, the Food and Nutrition Administration, or any state or local WIC agency.</p>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>We organize public information: WIC clinic locations gathered from public locator sources, the official income eligibility guidelines as published in the Federal Register each year, and practical application guides. Everything is free, and we never ask for personal information.</p>
  <h2>What we DON'T do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enroll anyone in WIC — only your local agency can, at a certification appointment.</li>
    <li>Collect applications, documents or personal data of any kind.</li>
    <li>Guarantee clinic hours or availability — always confirm by phone.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Sources and methodology</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Clinic directory:</strong> public clinic locator data, refreshed periodically. Clinics open, move and close — phone confirmation is always the final word.</li>
    <li><strong>Income limits:</strong> the USDA's annual notice in the Federal Register (2026-2027 cycle, effective July 1, 2026), checked against state agency publications.</li>
    <li><strong>Program rules:</strong> USDA FNA regulations and official FAQs.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Funding</h2>
  <p>The site is supported by advertising (Google AdSense), clearly distinguishable from content and with no influence on it.</p>
</main>
</Base>
